## [Mozilla CA certificate bundle](https://curl.se/docs/caextract.html)

`resources/resfile/ca-bundle.crt` carries the root certificates curl distributes
as `cacert.pem`, extracted from the Mozilla CA store (158 certificates at the
time of writing). It is what makes device-local HTTPS (git, extension download)
validate instead of failing with "unable to get local issuer certificate"; see
`launch_app.rs` setting `SSL_CERT_FILE`.

The bundle is distributed under the Mozilla Public License 2.0. The full text is
available at <https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/>; individual certificates carry their
own terms inside the bundle (each entry is preceded by a comment naming the CA).

